            <ArticleTitle>Bone scanning for the evaluation of knee prosthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Twenty-six knees were scanned after total replacement to evaluate the relationship between bone scan, pain, the presence of a radiolucent line at the bone-cement interface and loosening. A radiolucent line was often accompanied by an increased uptake over the affected condyle, but there was no significant relationship with pain or loosening.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
